      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manly%2C_Queensland"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The suburb was named Manly after the famous New South Wales beach, not after a local person.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manly%2C_Queensland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the Cleveland railway line opened in 1889, the station was christened Manly instead of Wyvernleigh.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.queenslandplaces.com.au/manly"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Manly Boat Harbour spans 41.8 hectares and lies just south of Norfolk Point.",
